+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** Reference-Checking v1 amendments register A5 changes the reference-check trigger from "shortlist" to "viewing": a new `application_status` value `'viewed'` (added `AFTER 'shortlisted'`) marks that the viewing has been carried out, and RC2.3 will fire reference-check creation on the transition INTO `viewed`. Before the trigger (RC2.3) can exist, `viewed` must be a first-class status that round-trips through the schema, every codec, the PATCH endpoint, and the status stepper / pills / leaderboard — end to end. This story is that plumbing.
+
+**Approach:** One additive enum migration (`ADD VALUE 'viewed' AFTER 'shortlisted'`), the `Viewed` variant threaded through the shared `ApplicationStatus` type + its three codec functions, the server `parse_status` accepting `"viewed"` (incl. the 400 message), a Squirrel regen so `sql.ApplicationStatus` carries `Viewed`, and the client stepper/pills/leaderboard/filters rendering `viewed` in the house semantic set (navy) without breaking. No trigger logic, no reference-check creation — that is RC2.3.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Migration is additive only: `ALTER TYPE application_status ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS 'viewed' AFTER 'shortlisted'` (the `auto_closed` enum-migration precedent, `IF NOT EXISTS` for idempotency, `AFTER 'shortlisted'` per A5 + the AC). 14-digit timestamp prefix, newer than `20260802120000` (the current latest migration on develop).
+- No trigger function in THIS migration references `'viewed'` — Postgres forbids referencing a newly-added enum value in the same transaction that added it (the `auto_closed` two-migration split reason). RC2.3 will add the viewed-trigger logic in its own later migration. rc2-2 adds the enum value only.
+- Shared `ApplicationStatus` gains a `Viewed` constructor; `encode_status` / `status_from_string` / `status_decoder` each gain the `"viewed"` ↔ `Viewed` arm. `status_from_string`'s total-inverse fallback comment already names "six values" — update to seven.
+- Server `parse_status` gains `"viewed" -> Ok(sql.Viewed)`; the `InvalidStatus` 400 message lists `viewed` alongside `under_review, shortlisted, approved, rejected`. The PATCH flow (`apply_status_update`) is unchanged — it already writes the `StatusChanged` audit row for any accepted status, and `maybe_send_shortlist_notification` has a `_ -> Nil` default so `viewed` correctly no-ops (RC2.3 hooks the reference trigger there).
+- Client stepper: progression becomes **Submitted → Reviewing → Shortlisted → Viewed → Approved** (5 stops; Reject + AutoClosed unchanged as terminal rows). Rank: Submitted=1, UnderReview=2, Shortlisted=3, **Viewed=4**, Approved=5 (Rejected/AutoClosed=0). `pipeline()`, `decode_status`, `label_for_slug_opt`, `slug_for_index`, `clamp_focus` (now 0..4), `focus_index_for_status`, and `stop_tone` all gain the viewed stop.
+- **House semantic set (brand doc "Application Status Pills"):** Submitted=slate, UnderReview=**navy**, Shortlisted=**amber**, Viewed=**navy**, Approved=**teal**, Rejected=red, AutoClosed=slate. `viewed` is navy = the in-progress colour, per the AC. This matches the existing detail-page pill (`application_detail.view_status_pill`) and the stepper's `stop_tone`, which ALREADY follow the brand doc.
+- The shared `status_pill.gleam` (leaderboard + comparison) is brought INTO the house semantic set as part of this story: it had drifted (UnderReview was amber, Shortlisted was `score-strong`). Aligning it is required for the AC's described set ("amber shortlisted … teal approved") to be true on the leaderboard surface, and makes all three pill surfaces (detail header / leaderboard / comparison) consistent. `score-strong` is `#2D8A7E` == teal, so Approved is visually unchanged; UnderReview (amber→navy) and Shortlisted (teal→amber) gain their brand-correct colours.
+- No em-dashes in any user-facing copy (RT global ban, CI-guarded). Status labels, stepper, pills — em-dash-free.
+- Migration runs against the local Docker test DB only; Squirrel runs against the local test DB directly (`cd server && DATABASE_URL=… gleam run -m squirrel`), NEVER staging/production and NEVER via `run_squirrel.sh` (it sources `.env` and points at staging).
+
+**Ask First:** recolouring a status the brand doc names differently than implemented here; adding a viewed-specific affordance (Next Step strip, trigger) — those belong to RC2.3+.
+
+**Never:** no reference-check creation / trigger logic (RC2.3); no new API route (the existing PATCH `/applications/:id/status` accepts `viewed` via `parse_status`); no edits to `reference_call` / consent / attestation schemas; no `DROP`/`RENAME` on `application_status` (expand-only); no `let assert` in production code; no JS FFI; no em-dashes in copy.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|---------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Migration idempotent | `ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS 'viewed'` run twice | Second run is a no-op; enum order keeps `viewed` after `shortlisted` | N/A (IF NOT EXISTS) |
+| Codec round-trip (shared) | `Viewed` | `encode_status(Viewed)="viewed"`; `status_from_string("viewed")=Viewed`; `status_decoder` succeeds on `"viewed"` | unknown string → `Submitted` fallback (from_string) / decode failure (decoder) |
+| Server PATCH accepts viewed | `{"status":"viewed"}` on a live application | 200 `{data:{status:"viewed"}}`; `audit_log` `StatusChanged` row written (from=prev, to="viewed") | owned/archived vacancy → 403/422 as today |
+| Server PATCH rejects unknown | `{"status":"nonsense"}` | 400 `InvalidStatus`, message lists `under_review, shortlisted, viewed, approved, rejected` | `parse_status` → Error |
+| Stepper renders 5 stops | application `status=Viewed` | 5-stop pipeline; Viewed stop active (navy); Submitted/Reviewing/Shortlisted completed (✓); Approved upcoming | terminal statuses still render muted rows |
+| Direction maths | click Viewed from Shortlisted | `Forward` (immediate dispatch); from Approved → Viewed is `Backward` (confirm modal) | rank compare |
+| Leaderboard pill | row with `status=Viewed` | navy "Viewed" pill; appears under "All" and score filters; not under "Shortlisted" filter | N/A |
+| Sweep nudge (out of scope) | approve A, a viewed B remains | B is NOT counted as "remaining to reject" (viewed defaults to terminal-for-sweep) — deliberate, documented | no bulk-reject of engaged applicants in rc2-2 |
+| Comparison CTA | viewed app in compare dock | "Contact" action (merged with Shortlisted arm — navigates to detail) | N/A |
