+## Design Notes
+
+- **Why recolour the shared `status_pill.gleam` (not just add viewed):** the AC describes the house semantic set as "amber shortlisted … teal approved". The detail-page pill (`application_detail.view_status_pill`) and the stepper already follow the brand doc's canonical "Application Status Pills" table (UnderReview=navy, Shortlisted=amber, Approved=teal). The shared leaderboard/comparison pill had drifted (UnderReview=amber, Shortlisted/Approved=`score-strong`). Adding only `viewed=navy` would leave the leaderboard pill internally inconsistent with the AC's described set and the other two surfaces. Aligning it (3 lines) makes all three consistent and brand-compliant. `score-strong` is `#2D8A7E` == teal, so Approved is visually identical; only UnderReview (amber→navy) and Shortlisted (teal→amber) change, both INTO brand compliance. Not a load-bearing contract change (no URL/API/shape impact) — documented here, no BREAKING prefix.
+- **Sweep nudge / bulk-reject deliberately exclude viewed (rc2-2):** `sweep_nudge_banner.is_non_terminal` and `bulk_reject_by_ids.sql` are left as-is, so a `viewed` applicant is NOT counted as "remaining to reject" after an approval and is NOT bulk-rejected. Rationale: a viewed applicant is one the landlord has engaged with (arranged a viewing); auto-rejecting them via a one-click sweep is higher-harm than leaving them for individual decision. This is context-dependent (a viewed app IS non-terminal for comparison-selection in `application_row`, which uses a `_ -> True` default) — different question, different right answer. RC2.3/RC3 (the reference lifecycle) is the natural home to revisit sweep semantics once reference rows exist on viewed apps.
+- **Comparison CTA for viewed = "Contact" (merged with Shortlisted):** viewed is post-shortlist, pre-approval; "Contact" (navigate to detail, where viewed-specific UI lands in RC2.3+) is the right next action. No new comparison UX invented.
+- **Two navy stops in the stepper (Reviewing + Viewed):** both are "in-progress" phases; the brand doc has exactly four status colours (slate/navy/amber/teal/red) and the AC assigns viewed=navy. The label + position disambiguate the active stop. Acceptable and brand-faithful.
+- **Test-DB port:** sibling worktrees hold 54321/54322/54323; this story runs its own container on 54324 (`rt-rc2-2-test-db`) for migration + Squirrel + integration, torn down afterwards.
+- **Server side is minimal:** `parse_status` + the 400 message are the only hand-edits; `apply_status_update` and `maybe_send_shortlist_notification` already handle any accepted status via `_ ->` defaults. The viewed reference-trigger hook lands in RC2.3 at `maybe_send_shortlist_notification`'s call site.
